{"name":"Soft Boiled","hex":"#ffb737","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"soft boiled","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative spelling of soft-boiled."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soft_boiled"}],"entries":[{"title":"Soft Boiled","blocks":[{"text":"Soft Boiled is a 1923 American silent comedy Western film written and directed by John G. Blystone. The film stars Tom Mix, Billie Dove, Joseph W. Girard, Lee Shumway, Tom Wilson, and Frank Beal. The film was released on August 26, 1923, by Fox Film Corporation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Soft_Boiled_%28SAYRE_14047%29.jpg/330px-Soft_Boiled_%28SAYRE_14047%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soft_Boiled","wikidata":"Q62076011"},{"title":"Boiling","blocks":[{"text":"Boiling or ebullition is the rapid phase transition from liquid to gas or vapour; the reverse of boiling is condensation. Boiling occurs when a liquid is heated to its boiling point, so that the vapour pressure of the liquid is equal to the pressure exerted on the liquid by the surrounding atmosphere. Boiling and evaporation are the two main forms of liquid vapourization."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Boilingkettle.jpg/330px-Boilingkettle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boiling","wikidata":"Q41716"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Flickr_-_cyclonebill_-_Pasta_%281%29.jpg/500px-Flickr_-_cyclonebill_-_Pasta_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Flickr_-_cyclonebill_-_Pasta_%281%29.jpg/1280px-Flickr_-_cyclonebill_-_Pasta_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://t